    "designDecisionsAndRationale": [
      "Atomic reservation binds task, exact session, lease, selected placement and launch token to fence stale and uncertain launches; the existing runner executes task work.",
      "The shared durable applier validates causality and replay; guard violations are persisted as an ordered batch before decisions.",
      "Reachable callee requirements and one fresh merged capability snapshot determine selected hosts before reservation; no silent local fallback.",
      "The bounded director uses a single ordinary child and persisted judged-work linkage; child success alone cannot accept work.",
      "Prove task-backed replacement behavior before removing legacy auto-improve; the accepted §17.7 plan is the only executable work package."
    ],
    "intentionalTradeoffs": [
      "Keep tightly coupled prerequisite, dispatch, director and removal work in one serial plan to protect shared files and evidence.",
      "Use existing runner, store, adapter and distributed paths; preserve explicit unverified capability status where probes fail."
    ],
    "supportedEdgeCases": [
      "Dependency/version races, capacity waits, stale launch tokens, uncertainty fencing, pending cancellation before launch and during terminal persistence, reopen/replay and exact canceled-session acknowledgment.",
      "Cumulative budgets, repeated findings, inactivity, deterministic simultaneous violations, last-admitted-attempt completion, and human-required acceptance.",
      "Reachable called workflows, unresolved or unavailable hosts, worker loss, stale/foreign judged-work linkage, invalid director output, exhausted child admission and exact single-charge accounting."
    ],
    "outOfScopeEdgeCases": [
